  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BAC CR Green</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The most significant, expected project-level outcome will be: increased access to MSMEs including WSMEs and climate finance. Beyond this outcome, IFC anticipates the Project will promote greater market sustainability by incentivizing other financial institutions to increase their climate lending.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed investment consists of an up to US$230 million financing package for Banco BAC San Jos&#xE9;, S.A. (BAC CR or the Bank) in Costa Rica, consisting of: (i) an up to US$200 million senior unsecured loan for IFCs own account (IFC A Loan); and (ii) a Global Trade Finance Program (GTFP) unfunded guarantee line of up to US$30 million. The loan will have a 5-year tenor and 2-year grace period and will be used to support the growth of the Banks climate and micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) portfolios, with at least 40% destined to finance climate sub-projects, and at least 30% will be allocated to women-owned businesses (WSMEs) (the Project).</narrative>
  </description>
